abstract: >-
  Stund is an activity-enriched collaborative workspace mediated by
  artificial intelligence. Its Webstrates-based web client provides a
  shared, malleable 2D canvas built on tldraw and an AI chat whose
  agents can act on the canvas, create widgets and processors, and
  query the activity history. Its activity session server,
  SessionHistoryServer, records collaborative activity as queryable,
  timed events: voice, video, notes and edits land as events on a
  shared timeline, media is recorded via WebRTC ingest into Matroska
  files that are servable while still growing, and pluggable
  processors (including sandboxed JavaScript and OpenAI-compatible LLM
  processors) derive new events, live or over recorded sessions.
